  "daily_brief": {
    "story_1": {
      "kicker": "India | Economy",
      "headline": "RBI bulletin: Indian economy performed well",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The Reserve Bank of India has released its latest bulletin indicating that the Indian economy performed well despite various global headwinds. The financial and external sectors continue to draw strength from a resilient domestic economic framework.",
        "Policymakers noted that steady domestic activity has helped cushion the broader system against international shocks and external market volatility."
      ],
      "image": {
        "url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Tower_and_building_of_Reserve_Bank_of_India%2C_Mumbai_04.jpg/960px-Tower_and_building_of_Reserve_Bank_of_India%2C_Mumbai_04.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail",
        "alt": "Tower and building of Reserve Bank of India, Mumbai 04"
      }
    },
    "story_2": {
      "kicker": "Global | Geopolitics",
      "headline": "Economy resilient with downside risks",
      "paragraphs": [
        "According to the RBI bulletin, the domestic economy remains resilient overall, though notable downside risks persist. These risks include ongoing tensions and conflicts emanating from the West Asia region.",
        "Analysts continue to monitor these geopolitical flashpoints closely for potential spillover effects on commodity prices and international supply chains."
      ]
    },
    "story_3": {
      "kicker": "Markets | Equities",
      "headline": "India Equity Indices on Losing Streak",
      "paragraphs": [
        "India equity indices have extended their downward pressure, marking a losing streak for the seventh straight week. Market participants continue to weigh shifting macroeconomic signals against prevailing valuations."
      ]
    },
    "also_today": {
      "items": [
        "Forex reserves fall by USD 14.88 billion to USD 765.90 billion in the week ended September 18.",
